      },
      {
        "number": 21,
        "question": "What is the purpose of helm lint?",
        "answer": "The helm lint command checks a Helm chart for common structural and formatting problems. It helps identify issues such as missing required chart metadata, invalid chart structure, and some template-related problems.\n\nIt is commonly included in CI pipelines to catch chart issues before packaging or deployment.\n\nFor example, a pull request that changes a Helm chart can run helm lint as an automated validation step. Linting is useful, but it does not prove that every rendered resource will work correctly in a real Kubernetes cluster."
      },
      {
        "number": 22,
        "question": "What is the purpose of helm package?",
