        "answer": "A StatefulSet manages applications that require stable Pod identities, predictable ordering, and often persistent storage. Pods receive stable ordinal identities and can use persistent volume claims associated with each replica. It is commonly used for stateful systems such as databases and clustered services when their storage and recovery requirements match StatefulSet behavior."
      },
      {
        "number": 4,
        "question": "What is a DaemonSet in Kubernetes?",
        "answer": "A DaemonSet ensures that a copy of a Pod runs on each eligible node or on nodes selected by its scheduling rules. It is commonly used for node-level services such as log collectors, monitoring agents, and network components. For example, a logging agent can run on every worker node to collect container logs."
      },
      {
        "number": 5,
