      },
      {
        "number": 8,
        "question": "What is an Ingress in Kubernetes?",
        "answer": "Ingress is an API resource that defines HTTP and HTTPS routing rules from external clients to Kubernetes Services. An Ingress controller must be installed to implement those rules, because the Ingress resource alone does not provide traffic handling. For example, host and path rules can route `/api` requests to an API service and `/shop` requests to a frontend service."
      },
      {
        "number": 9,
        "question": "What is an Ingress controller?",
