      {
        "number": 17,
        "question": "How do you change a Git remote URL?",
        "answer": "Use `git remote set-url origin NEW_URL` to update the URL associated with the origin remote. Then verify it with `git remote -v` and test connectivity using an appropriate fetch command. This is useful when a repository moves to a new server or changes from HTTPS to SSH access."
      },
      {
        "number": 18,
        "question": "What is a detached HEAD state in Git?",
