      {
        "number": 13,
        "question": "What is the purpose of the EKS aws-auth ConfigMap and what is its modern alternative?",
        "answer": "The aws-auth ConfigMap was historically used to map IAM users and roles to Kubernetes usernames and groups for EKS cluster access. Newer EKS access management supports access entries, which provide an AWS-managed method to associate IAM principals with cluster access policies or Kubernetes groups. The correct mechanism depends on the cluster authentication mode and existing configuration. When access fails, inspect the cluster's authentication configuration, access entries, associated policies, and any legacy aws-auth mappings. Do not create conflicting identity mappings without understanding the active mode. Plan migrations carefully, preserve administrator access, and validate the new identity with kubectl before removing legacy configuration."
