        "answer": "CrashLoopBackOff means a container repeatedly exits and Kubernetes is delaying subsequent restart attempts. Start with kubectl get pods -n NAMESPACE and kubectl describe pod POD -n NAMESPACE. Inspect the previous container logs using kubectl logs POD -n NAMESPACE --previous, because the current container may have already restarted. Check exit codes, startup commands, environment variables, mounted configuration, Secrets, probes, resource limits, and application dependencies. Exit code 137 may indicate a process was killed, often due to memory pressure, while an application error may produce another exit code. Compare the restart timeline with deployments and configuration changes. Correct the application or runtime cause, then verify stable readiness and reduced restart counts."
