        "number": 27,
        "question": "How do you troubleshoot EKS pods that cannot communicate with services in another namespace?",
        "answer": "First verify that the destination Service exists and has ready endpoints using kubectl get svc,endpoints -n TARGET_NAMESPACE. Check the service name, namespace, port, targetPort, and protocol used by the client. Test DNS resolution from the source pod and then test connectivity to the Service or endpoint IP. Inspect NetworkPolicies, security groups for pods if enabled, VPC CNI behavior, and application-level authentication or TLS requirements. Determine whether the failure affects one pod, one namespace, or the entire cluster. Review recent policy and deployment changes. Correct the service selector, port, DNS, network policy, or application configuration and validate communication from the actual source workload."
