        "number": 29,
        "question": "How do you troubleshoot EKS applications that experience intermittent network timeouts?",
        "answer": "Intermittent timeouts can originate from pod resource pressure, node networking, DNS latency, connection tracking limits, security controls, load balancer health, or a slow downstream dependency. Compare failures by pod, node, availability zone, destination, and timestamp. Inspect application logs, pod restarts, CPU and memory, node conditions, VPC CNI metrics, CoreDNS health, and relevant AWS network configuration. Test repeated connections from affected and healthy pods to determine whether the issue follows a node or destination. Review recent deployments, security group changes, route updates, and traffic increases. Apply a targeted correction and monitor error rate and latency over a representative period before closing the incident."
