        "answer": "A common EKS monitoring architecture collects cluster and workload metrics through Prometheus-compatible scraping and visualizes them in Grafana. Teams monitor node capacity, pod CPU and memory, restart counts, scheduling failures, API behavior, network health, and application service-level indicators. Deploy collectors and exporters using a supported Helm chart or platform-managed approach, and configure scrape targets through ServiceMonitors or equivalent mechanisms when using the Prometheus Operator. Verify that targets are healthy and metric labels identify the correct cluster, namespace, and workload. Build alerts for user-impacting symptoms and infrastructure saturation. Secure access to monitoring endpoints and ensure the monitoring stack has persistent storage, resource limits, and an independent alert delivery path."
