        "number": 39,
        "question": "How do you plan a safe EKS production node group migration?",
        "answer": "A node group migration should begin with workload inventory, Kubernetes and AMI compatibility checks, capacity planning, PodDisruptionBudget review, and a rollback plan. Create the replacement node group with the required labels, taints, networking, IAM role, and instance configuration. Verify that new nodes register as Ready and that critical DaemonSets and system pods run correctly. Move workloads gradually using scheduling controls and controlled draining of old nodes. Monitor application availability, pod placement, storage attachment, load balancer targets, and node-level errors. Keep enough spare capacity to avoid simultaneous disruption. Remove the old group only after workload owners confirm health and the migration has passed its validation window."
