        "question": "What is Sonatype Nexus Repository and how is it used in a production DevOps pipeline?",
        "answer": "Sonatype Nexus Repository is an artifact repository manager used to store, proxy, and distribute software components and build artifacts. It can host internal releases and snapshots, proxy public repositories such as Maven Central, and provide repository groups that simplify client configuration. In a production CI/CD pipeline, Jenkins can download dependencies through Nexus, build an application, and publish approved JAR, WAR, npm, Docker, or other supported artifacts to the appropriate repository format. This improves control over artifact availability, versioning, and access. Production operations include backup, storage monitoring, permissions, cleanup policies, repository health checks, and protection of released artifacts."
