        "number": 4,
        "question": "What is JQL and how do you use it to identify delayed DevOps work?",
        "answer": "Jira Query Language, or JQL, is used to search for issues based on fields, operators, and functions. A team can query issues by project, assignee, status, priority, labels, sprint, or dates. For example, project = DEVOPS AND statusCategory != Done AND created <= -7d can help identify older unresolved work, subject to the project's field configuration. A query such as project = DEVOPS AND priority = Highest AND resolution IS EMPTY can identify unresolved high-priority work. In production operations, JQL supports incident tracking, aging reports, release readiness, and workload reviews. Validate field names and project permissions when a query returns unexpected results, and save frequently used searches as filters."
