        "question": "Q33. Explain Kubernetes certificate rotation and how expired API server, kubelet, or webhook certificates can affect cluster operations.",
        "answer": "Kubernetes uses certificates for authenticated communication between control-plane components, nodes, and some integrations. An expired or incorrectly trusted certificate can prevent kubelets from communicating with the API server, cause API clients to fail TLS verification, or break admission webhooks. Inspect certificate expiration, issuer, subject, SANs, trust chains, and the component configuration that references each certificate. The exact renewal process depends on whether the cluster is managed by a cloud provider, kubeadm, or another distribution. Back up relevant configuration and follow the supported rotation procedure rather than replacing files manually without updating dependent components. Validate API access, node registration, webhook calls, and component health after rotation, and establish expiry monitoring before the next renewal window."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q34. How would you troubleshoot Kubernetes rollout failures caused by readiness probes, startup probes, and PodDisruptionBudgets?",
        "answer": "Inspect Deployment rollout status, ReplicaSet events, Pod conditions, container logs, and probe failure messages. A readiness probe failure removes a Pod from normal Service endpoint selection, while a liveness probe failure can cause a container restart. A startup probe gives slow-starting applications additional time before liveness and readiness checks take effect. Incorrect paths, ports, schemes, thresholds, timeouts, or dependency assumptions can make healthy applications appear unavailable. PodDisruptionBudgets can also prevent voluntary evictions when insufficient replicas are available. Correct probe behavior based on actual application startup and serving semantics, and ensure replica capacity satisfies availability goals. Validate a rolling update under load and confirm that old replicas are removed only after new replicas become Ready."
      },
