      {
        "question": "Q23. Explain Jenkins Pipeline CPS execution and how serialization problems can cause pipeline failures after controller restarts.",
        "answer": "Jenkins Pipeline uses a continuation-passing style execution model that allows Pipeline state to be persisted and resumed across controller restarts. Pipeline execution state may be serialized at suspension points, so retaining non-serializable objects in script variables can cause persistence failures. Common examples include keeping complex library objects, open streams, or certain Java objects in long-lived variables. Keep Pipeline state simple and serializable, use supported Pipeline steps, and move complex computation into carefully designed shared-library methods or external tools. When a Pipeline fails during persistence, inspect the full stack trace and identify the object or method involved. Test restart and resume behavior with representative jobs before promoting shared-library changes across production pipelines."
