        "answer": "Jenkins plugins extend controller functionality through integrations, Pipeline steps, SCM support, authentication, agents, and user-interface features. Plugins have dependencies and compatibility requirements with specific Jenkins core versions and sometimes with other plugins. Before upgrading, inventory installed plugins, identify critical job dependencies, review security advisories and release notes, and test the intended plugin set in a staging controller using a recent configuration backup. Upgrade in a controlled sequence and validate representative pipelines, authentication, agent connections, webhooks, and credential access. Avoid unreviewed bulk upgrades directly in production. Maintain a rollback plan that accounts for plugin binaries and persisted configuration compatibility, and remove unused plugins to reduce attack surface and operational complexity."
