        "question": "Q27. Explain how to implement Jenkins shared libraries safely for reusable enterprise Pipeline standards.",
        "answer": "Jenkins shared libraries centralize reusable Pipeline functions, standard stages, deployment procedures, and organizational controls. A library can be configured globally or at folder scope, and its version or branch should be controlled so builds use a known implementation. Trusted libraries require especially strict repository permissions because their code may run with elevated Jenkins capabilities. Keep interfaces stable, document inputs and outputs, validate parameters, and avoid exposing credentials through return values or logs. Test library changes with representative jobs and maintain versioned releases or pinned revisions for critical pipelines. Use libraries for reusable policy and workflow logic, while keeping application-specific decisions explicit in the consuming repository."
