      {
        "answer": "Define repository ownership, naming, access, branching, review, signing, secret scanning, retention, and release-tagging standards. Provide reusable templates and automated policy checks so teams can follow the standard without manual configuration. Monitor repository health, large-file growth, inactive maintainers, permission exceptions, and CI integration failures. Establish backup and recovery expectations for critical repositories and test restoration. Maintain documented procedures for credential exposure, accidental history rewriting, repository migration, and account compromise. Review governance effectiveness regularly using measurable compliance and developer-experience indicators.",
