        "question": "Q31. How do protected branches improve CI/CD security and reliability?",
        "answer": "Protected branches restrict direct pushes, require pull requests, enforce reviews, and can require successful status checks before merging. Configure mandatory CI jobs, code-owner approval, signed commits where appropriate, and restrictions on force pushes and deletion. Ensure administrators and automation accounts are governed by explicit policies rather than broad bypasses. Periodically test the rules with normal developer and service accounts. Protection is effective only when required checks represent meaningful tests and cannot be skipped by untrusted workflows."
