        "question": "Q32. How do you troubleshoot a shallow clone that causes a pipeline to fail?",
        "answer": "A shallow clone downloads limited commit history, which can break tools that calculate version numbers, changelogs, merge bases, or tags. Inspect the checkout configuration and commands such as git rev-parse --is-shallow-repository and git describe --tags. Fetch the required history or tags, or configure the CI checkout depth appropriately. Avoid downloading the entire history unnecessarily if pipeline performance is important. Re-run the versioning and release steps to confirm that the expected commit metadata is available."
      },
