        "question": "Q34. How do you design a Git branching strategy for multiple release environments?",
        "answer": "Choose a branching model that matches release frequency and deployment controls. A trunk-based model with short-lived branches and feature flags suits frequent continuous delivery, while release branches can support controlled maintenance of multiple supported versions. Define how fixes flow between development, release, and production branches, and automate merges where safe. Protect important branches, require review and CI checks, and tag every production release. Avoid long-lived branches that accumulate large, difficult-to-review differences."
      },
