        "question": "Q35. How do you audit and improve Git repository security in an enterprise environment?",
        "answer": "Review repository visibility, branch protections, collaborator permissions, deploy keys, personal access tokens, webhooks, and CI service accounts. Enforce least privilege, MFA or SSO policies, secret scanning, dependency scanning, and signed release artifacts where required. Audit access and sensitive changes regularly, rotate credentials, and remove stale accounts. Protect workflow definitions because untrusted pipeline changes can expose secrets. Validate controls through periodic access tests and retain logs that support incident investigation and compliance reviews."
