      {
        "question": "Q12. What are sync waves and hooks in ArgoCD?",
        "answer": "Sync waves order resources during synchronization using annotations that assign resources to different wave numbers. They help deploy dependencies in a controlled sequence, such as namespaces before workloads or configuration before applications. Resource hooks support lifecycle actions such as pre-sync validation, sync-time jobs, and post-sync verification. Hooks need clear deletion policies and timeout behavior. Avoid relying on ordering alone for application readiness; validate dependencies and health conditions explicitly before promoting a production deployment."
