      },
      {
        "question": "Q20. How would you design an enterprise ArgoCD GitOps operating model?",
        "answer": "Use protected Git repositories as the source of truth, controlled ArgoCD projects, environment-specific destinations, and reusable ApplicationSet templates. Enforce pull-request reviews, policy checks, image provenance controls, and secure secret integration. Apply automated sync selectively, define health checks and progressive delivery, and monitor reconciliation failures and drift. Establish clear ownership for platform and application teams, audit changes, and test disaster recovery. Standardize promotion from development to production while preserving traceability to the exact Git revision."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q21. How would you design Argo CD Application health assessments for a platform containing custom Kubernetes resources?",
        "answer": "Argo CD evaluates resource health using built-in assessments for supported Kubernetes kinds and Lua-based custom health checks for resources that need organization-specific interpretation. In a production platform, define custom health logic for operators such as databases, messaging systems, and service-mesh controllers when their CRDs expose meaningful status conditions. Configure the checks centrally through Argo CD configuration and inspect fields such as status.conditions, observedGeneration, readyReplicas, and controller-reported readiness. A resource should not be reported healthy merely because it exists; the check must distinguish progressing, healthy, degraded, and unknown states. Test the Lua logic against representative healthy, progressing, failed, missing-status, and stale-generation objects before rollout. Deploy the configuration to a non-production Argo CD instance first, then monitor Application health transitions and compare them with the actual controller state. Keep custom checks version-controlled, reviewed, and covered by upgrade tests because Kubernetes APIs and CRD status schemas can evolve. Document ownership and alerting behavior so platform teams can diagnose incorrect health assessments without masking real deployment failures."
