        "question": "Q30. What is the safest way to perform an Argo CD version upgrade in a production environment?",
        "answer": "Begin by reviewing the supported upgrade path, release notes, deprecated APIs, security advisories, and compatibility requirements for Kubernetes, Redis, repository plugins, and custom health checks. Back up Argo CD configuration, repository and cluster Secret definitions through an approved secure process, RBAC policies, and Application source-of-truth data. Test the target version against representative Applications in a staging control plane, including Helm rendering, Kustomize builds, custom plugins, sync waves, hooks, and health assessments. Upgrade using the documented deployment method and maintain a rollback plan that accounts for controller state and configuration changes, not just container image tags. Monitor component readiness, repository connectivity, reconciliation queues, and Application health during rollout. Avoid upgrading all production control-plane instances simultaneously when a staged strategy is available. Confirm that Applications continue reconciling correctly and document any required configuration migration."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q31. How would you investigate an Argo CD sync operation that fails because Kubernetes admission policies reject a resource?",
        "answer": "Identify the exact resource and admission error from the sync operation details and Kubernetes events. Determine whether the rejection comes from a validating admission policy, webhook, Pod Security enforcement, quota, or another cluster control. Compare the rendered manifest with the policy requirements, including security context, image registry, resource requests, labels, and prohibited capabilities. Inspect webhook availability and latency if the error indicates a timeout or internal webhook failure rather than a policy violation. Correct the manifest in Git or coordinate a controlled policy update through the platform governance process; do not bypass admission controls simply to make the sync succeed. Re-run validation with the same API-server rules where possible, then synchronize and confirm the live resource satisfies the policy. Add pre-merge policy checks and clear error reporting so teams can detect violations before production deployment."
