      {
        "question": "Q32. How do you design reliable disaster recovery for an Argo CD control plane?",
        "answer": "Make Git the authoritative source for Application definitions, project configuration, RBAC policy, and deployment configuration so the control plane can be reconstructed. Back up required Kubernetes Secrets, repository credentials, cluster registration data, and external dependencies using encrypted, access-controlled backup processes. Document the Argo CD installation version, configuration, plugin images, certificates, DNS, ingress, and secret-management dependencies. In a recovery environment, restore the control plane, reconnect target clusters, validate repository access, and allow Applications to refresh and reconcile from their intended revisions. Be careful with automated sync during recovery: confirm that the restored Git state is the approved desired state before allowing changes to propagate. Test recovery regularly, measure recovery time, and verify that credentials and certificates remain valid. A backup is not proven until a restore exercise demonstrates that Applications can be reconstructed and safely reconciled."
