      },
      {
        "question": "Q18. How would you implement multi-window, multi-burn-rate SLO alerts using Prometheus?",
        "answer": "A burn-rate alert compares the observed error-budget consumption rate with the allowed rate implied by the SLO. A multi-window approach checks both a short window and a longer window so that fast incidents can be detected without reacting to isolated noise. PromQL first calculates the error ratio using consistent request and error metrics, then compares it with burn-rate thresholds derived from the SLO objective and alerting policy. Use separate labels and annotations to identify the service and affected objective. Validate traffic volume, missing series, counter resets, and the relationship between alert windows before routing pages to production responders."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q19. Prometheus queries are slow after the number of monitored services increased. How would you diagnose and reduce query load?",
