        "question": "Q2. Explain Grafana provisioning and how you would manage dashboards and data sources through GitOps.",
        "answer": "Grafana provisioning allows data sources, dashboards, alert rules, and other supported resources to be defined declaratively in files. A GitOps workflow stores these definitions in version control, validates them in pull requests, and deploys approved changes through CI/CD or configuration management. This reduces manual drift and makes environments repeatable. Teams should define ownership, folder placement, stable identifiers, and environment-specific variables carefully. Provisioning behavior can overwrite or conflict with UI-managed changes, so establish whether resources are code-owned or manually managed and test the deployment process in a non-production Grafana instance."
