        "question": "Q3. What are the recommended security practices for managing Grafana data source credentials?",
        "answer": "Data source credentials should be stored using Grafana secure settings or an approved external secret-management integration rather than embedded in dashboard JSON or source control. Restrict who can create and edit data sources, use least-privilege service credentials, and rotate secrets according to the organization policy. Avoid exposing credentials through provisioning files, debug logs, screenshots, or browser-visible variables. Use TLS for connections to Grafana and data sources, and verify that backups and deployment artifacts protect encrypted secret material. Test credential rotation and access revocation before relying on them during an incident."
