      },
      {
        "question": "Q24. What are the security considerations when configuring Grafana data source credentials?",
        "answer": "Treat data source credentials as sensitive secrets because they may grant access to production metrics, logs, traces, databases, or cloud services. Use dedicated service identities with the minimum read permissions required by each data source, and avoid reusing personal administrator credentials. Store secrets using Grafana's supported secure configuration mechanisms or an approved external secret-management integration. Restrict who can create or modify data sources and who can use them through dashboard permissions and organization controls. Ensure TLS verification is enabled for data source connections and rotate credentials according to policy. Never place tokens in dashboard JSON, query variables, URLs, or screenshots. Review data source access after team changes and test that users cannot access sensitive datasets through an overly privileged shared connection."
