      },
      {
        "question": "Q27. What is the difference between Grafana-managed alerting and data source-managed alerting, and how would you choose?",
        "answer": "Grafana-managed alert rules are evaluated by Grafana's alerting engine and can use supported data sources and expressions, while data source-managed rules are evaluated by the underlying monitoring system, such as Prometheus or Mimir. The choice depends on where rule ownership, evaluation, state management, and notification integration should reside. Centralizing rules in Grafana can simplify cross-data-source alerting and UI-based management, while source-managed rules can keep monitoring logic close to the metrics platform and its existing operational workflow. Avoid maintaining duplicate rules in both systems without a clear ownership model. Evaluate HA behavior, provisioning support, rule versioning, query compatibility, and notification routing. Test alert state transitions and recovery behavior during data source outages before choosing a production standard."
