      {
        "question": "Q1. Explain the architecture of Sonatype Nexus Repository Manager and how its major components work together.",
        "answer": "Nexus Repository Manager provides centralized storage and distribution for software components, packages, and container images. Its architecture includes repository definitions, blob stores, metadata databases, security and authorization services, scheduled tasks, and client-facing APIs. Developers and CI pipelines publish artifacts to hosted repositories, retrieve approved dependencies through proxy repositories, and use repository groups to access multiple repositories through one endpoint. The database stores repository configuration and metadata, while blob stores retain binary content. In production, administrators must monitor both metadata storage and blob capacity, protect the database and blob stores together during backups, and maintain repository access policies."
