        "question": "Q7. Explain how Nexus repository groups affect Maven dependency resolution and how you would troubleshoot an incorrect artifact version being downloaded.",
        "answer": "A Maven group presents multiple repositories through one URL, allowing a build to request dependencies without knowing the physical repository that contains each component. Resolution can be affected by repository membership, ordering, metadata, cached proxy responses, and the coordinates requested by the POM. To investigate an incorrect version, capture the exact group URL and coordinates, inspect the effective POM and dependency tree, and check which member repository supplied the artifact. Review proxy cache state and Maven local cache separately. Correct the repository configuration or dependency declaration, then validate from a clean or controlled client cache without deleting shared repository content blindly."
