      },
      {
        "question": "Q22. How would you design Jira workflows for a production incident management process?",
        "answer": "Model the actual incident lifecycle with clear states such as Open, Triage, In Progress, Mitigated, Resolved, and Closed. Define transitions with conditions, validators, and post-functions so that critical information is captured before an incident moves forward. Require impact, severity, affected service, incident commander, and relevant timestamps where appropriate. Use automation to notify responders, escalate overdue incidents, and create follow-up problem records. Keep emergency transitions available to authorized responders without bypassing auditability. Test the workflow with real incident scenarios and measure whether it improves response time, handoffs, and post-incident reporting."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q23. How would you troubleshoot Jira users who can access a project but cannot see specific issues?",
