      },
      {
        "question": "Q24. How would you manage Jira custom fields in a large instance to avoid performance and administration problems?",
        "answer": "Establish a field governance process before creating new custom fields. Search for existing fields with equivalent meaning, and define a consistent naming convention, field type, context, owner, and purpose. Restrict field contexts to the projects and issue types that need them instead of making every field globally available. Remove obsolete fields only after checking screens, workflows, filters, dashboards, automation rules, and integrations for dependencies. Review field usage and configuration periodically. Coordinate changes through testing and change control because excessive fields and broad contexts can increase administrative complexity and make issue screens harder to maintain."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q25. How would you build reliable Jira automation for cross-team issue handoffs?",
