        "question": "Q8. How would you troubleshoot intermittent HTTP 502 and 504 errors between Nginx or an AWS load balancer and Tomcat?",
        "answer": "First determine whether the proxy cannot connect to Tomcat, receives an invalid response, or waits longer than its configured timeout. Check Tomcat connector availability, application response times, thread saturation, connection limits, JVM pauses, and application exceptions. Review Nginx error logs or load-balancer target health and access logs, then correlate timestamps with Tomcat access and application logs. Test the backend directly from the proxy network using curl and inspect connection establishment and response timing. Verify proxy timeouts, keep-alive behavior, backend port, TLS settings, and health-check paths. Fix the limiting layer rather than simply increasing every timeout. Validate with concurrent requests and monitor 5xx rates and latency after the change."
