      {
        "question": "Q9. Explain Tomcat connection pooling with JNDI DataSource configuration and how to prevent database connection exhaustion.",
        "answer": "Tomcat can expose a database connection pool through a JNDI DataSource so web applications obtain connections without creating a new physical database connection for every request. Pool configuration includes properties such as maximum active connections, minimum idle connections, validation behavior, connection wait time, and database driver configuration, depending on the pooling implementation. A pool that is too small can cause request threads to wait, while an oversized pool can overwhelm the database. Diagnose exhaustion by checking active and idle connections, wait times, connection leaks, database session limits, and application transaction behavior. Ensure connections are returned in finally blocks or try-with-resources, configure validation appropriately, and load-test realistic concurrency."
