        "question": "Q11. Explain Tomcat graceful shutdown and how to prevent in-flight requests from being interrupted during deployments.",
        "answer": "A graceful shutdown aims to stop accepting new work while allowing existing requests and application tasks to finish within a controlled period. The exact behavior depends on Tomcat version, connector configuration, deployment topology, and the shutdown mechanism used. In a load-balanced environment, first remove the instance from new traffic and allow the load balancer's deregistration or connection-draining period to complete. Then stop Tomcat using the approved service-management procedure and verify that application threads and background executors terminate. Configure suitable request and shutdown timeouts, and ensure long-running jobs have explicit completion or recovery behavior. Test shutdown under realistic traffic and confirm that users do not experience avoidable connection resets."
