        "question": "Q31. How would you manage Tomcat session replication or session persistence across multiple application instances?",
        "answer": "First determine whether the application can be made stateless or whether it genuinely requires server-side HTTP session state. Stateless designs using signed tokens or externalized state often simplify horizontal scaling. If session replication is required, select a mechanism supported by the application architecture and Tomcat version, and verify its compatibility with the load balancer and cluster topology. Ensure session attributes are serializable when the chosen replication mechanism requires it, and avoid storing large objects or non-portable resources in sessions. Test node loss, rolling deployment, session expiration, and failover behavior. Monitor replication traffic, session size, and serialization errors. Document how sessions behave during maintenance and disaster recovery so users do not experience unexpected logouts or inconsistent state."
