      },
      {
        "question": "Q7. A production EBS volume is almost full and application writes are failing. What is the safe recovery process?",
        "answer": "Confirm filesystem utilization with df -h and identify large directories using du, while checking inode exhaustion with df -i. Review application logs, log rotation, temporary files, database growth, and backup artifacts to determine the cause. Do not delete unknown database or application files. If expansion is required, take an appropriate snapshot, modify the EBS volume size, wait for modification progress, and extend the partition and filesystem using the correct operating-system procedure. Verify mount points and application write access. Monitor filesystem and inode usage afterward, and implement capacity alerts, log retention, and storage growth reviews."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q8. A deployment causes an IAM AccessDenied error when an EC2 application accesses S3. How do you resolve it?",
