      },
      {
        "question": "Q10. A production deployment accidentally deletes an important CloudFormation-managed resource. How do you recover?",
        "answer": "Stop further stack changes and identify the stack event, change set, deletion policy, and exact resource state. Determine whether the resource is recoverable through service-native backups, snapshots, versioning, or retention settings. Do not immediately recreate resources with the same logical name because dependencies and data may be affected. Restore data or configuration through the documented recovery process, then reconcile the CloudFormation template and actual infrastructure state. Use drift detection and carefully reviewed change sets before applying another update. Confirm application functionality and data integrity. Prevent recurrence through stack termination protection, deletion policies for critical resources, code review, and production approval gates."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q11. A production Route 53 DNS change sends users to the wrong endpoint. What is your incident procedure?",
