      {
        "question": "Q24. A production EBS-backed database reports high disk latency during peak traffic. How would you diagnose it?",
        "answer": "Inspect EBS volume type, provisioned IOPS and throughput, queue length, burst balance where applicable, and CloudWatch volume metrics. Compare disk latency with database wait events, query patterns, CPU, memory, and transaction volume. Check whether the instance's EBS bandwidth limit is saturated even when the volume itself appears adequately provisioned. Identify large scans, checkpoint activity, backups, and competing workloads. Tune database I/O behavior and storage capacity based on measured demand. Test changes under representative load and monitor latency percentiles. Establish storage performance baselines and capacity alarms before peak periods."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q25. A production application fails after an IAM role policy was tightened. How do you identify the missing permission without over-permissioning?",
