      },
      {
        "question": "Q29. A production EKS workload cannot pull an image from ECR. What AWS-side checks would you perform?",
        "answer": "Inspect pod events and determine whether the failure is authentication, authorization, DNS, network, or image-name related. Verify the node instance role or configured image-pull identity has the required ECR authorization and image-layer download permissions. Check repository policy, account and region, image tag, and lifecycle policy. Confirm worker nodes can reach ECR API and registry endpoints through NAT or the required VPC endpoints, including S3 access for image layers. Review DNS and security-group rules. Correct the missing identity or network dependency and verify that a newly scheduled pod can pull the image."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q30. A production RDS Multi-AZ failover causes application errors. How would you reduce the impact?",
