      },
      {
        "question": "Q31. A production application is exposed to a sudden traffic flood. How would you protect the AWS environment?",
        "answer": "Determine whether the traffic is legitimate demand, abusive automation, or a denial-of-service event. Review ALB, CloudFront, WAF, and application request metrics, source patterns, and error rates. Apply managed or carefully tested WAF rate-based rules and appropriate AWS Shield protections based on architecture and service needs. Cache safe static content and protect expensive application endpoints. Scale only after confirming database and downstream capacity. Preserve logs and coordinate with security and incident response teams. Validate that protective rules block unwanted traffic without rejecting legitimate users, and conduct regular traffic-abuse simulations."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q32. A production AWS backup job reports success, but a restore attempt fails. What does the team do?",
