      {
        "question": "Q36. A production application experiences intermittent throttling from a managed AWS API. How would you handle it?",
        "answer": "Identify the throttled API operation, account and region, request rate, and service quota from application logs and CloudWatch metrics. Determine whether retries are synchronized or whether a traffic burst exceeds the service's limits. Implement exponential backoff with jitter, bounded retries, and idempotency for operations that may be repeated. Buffer non-urgent work through queues where appropriate and request a quota increase only after confirming the workload requirement. Monitor throttling and end-to-end processing delay. Validate that retries do not amplify the incident or create duplicate resources."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q37. A production AWS application has a sudden increase in cross-region data transfer charges. How would you isolate the source?",
