        "question": "Q1. A production Docker container exits unexpectedly during peak traffic. How would you investigate?",
        "answer": "Start with docker ps -a, docker inspect, and docker logs to identify the exit code, termination reason, timestamps, and final application messages. Check whether the container was killed by the kernel due to memory pressure, stopped by an operator, or exited because the application process failed. Review host CPU, memory, disk, and kernel logs, then correlate the event with traffic and recent deployments. Inspect restart policy and orchestration events. Preserve logs and diagnostic evidence before recreating the container. Fix the application or resource issue, validate under load, and configure restart behavior and monitoring without masking repeated crashes."
