      {
        "question": "Q2. A Docker container repeatedly restarts with exit code 137. What is your production troubleshooting approach?",
        "answer": "Exit code 137 commonly indicates termination by SIGKILL and may be associated with an out-of-memory kill, although it is not proof by itself. Inspect docker inspect for OOMKilled, memory limits, and restart count. Check host memory pressure, kernel OOM logs, container memory metrics, and application heap behavior. Compare the configured container memory limit with JVM or runtime memory settings. Identify leaks, large allocations, or concurrency spikes before increasing limits. Apply a measured resource adjustment or application fix, then test under representative load. Add memory utilization and OOM alerts and verify that the container remains stable."
