      {
        "question": "Q36. A production Docker application suffers from repeated failed requests because the container restart policy is misconfigured. What would you change?",
        "answer": "Inspect the restart policy, container exit history, application exit codes, and orchestration behavior. A restart policy can restore a process after an unexpected exit but cannot fix a deterministic application failure or dependency outage. Identify whether the container should use always, unless-stopped, on-failure, or an orchestrator-managed restart strategy based on service requirements. Ensure restart loops are observable and do not hide crash causes. Add health checks and alerting for repeated restarts. Test expected behavior during manual stops, host reboot, and application failure."
