      {
        "question": "Q1. A developer force-pushes to a shared production release branch and removes commits. How do you recover the branch?",
        "answer": "First stop further pushes and notify release owners so nobody builds from the damaged branch. Inspect git reflog, remote-tracking references, CI build metadata, and the repository hosting audit log to identify the last correct commit SHA. Fetch the remote and compare the damaged branch with the verified commit. After confirming the intended history with the team, restore the branch using a controlled revert or an authorized force update with lease protection. Do not guess the recovery SHA. Verify the branch, tags, and release pipeline, then enable branch protection and restrict force pushes."
