      {
        "question": "Q13. A Git submodule update breaks production builds because it checks out an unexpected revision. What would you investigate?",
        "answer": "Inspect the parent repository's recorded submodule gitlink SHA, .gitmodules URL, submodule branch settings, and CI checkout behavior. A submodule normally follows the commit recorded by the parent repository, not simply the latest commit on its remote branch. Verify that the expected submodule commit exists and that the CI identity can access it. Pin the intended revision through a reviewed parent-repository commit and test recursive checkout from a clean workspace. Record submodule versions in release metadata and validate dependencies before deployment."
