      },
      {
        "question": "Q17. A production repository receives an unexpected commit from an unknown account. How do you investigate?",
        "answer": "Preserve the commit SHA, author and committer metadata, push timestamp, affected branches, and repository audit logs. Determine which account or token performed the push and whether the identity was compromised or incorrectly authorized. Review the commit diff for malicious code, secrets, pipeline changes, and deployment triggers. Suspend the affected credential when justified and contain automated promotion. Revert unauthorized changes through a reviewed commit and verify deployed artifacts. Rotate exposed credentials, review branch protections, and investigate access logs before restoring normal release operations."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q18. Git hooks fail after a repository server upgrade and commits are no longer being validated. What would you do?",
