      },
      {
        "question": "Q36. Git operations slow down because the repository contains many stale remote-tracking branches. What would you do?",
        "answer": "Inspect branch count, repository size, server-side references, and CI scripts that create temporary branches. Determine whether stale refs are merely local remote-tracking references or actual remote branches still used by teams. Use git remote prune origin or fetch pruning for local stale references after confirming the remote is authoritative. Coordinate deletion of obsolete remote branches with their owners and preserve release branches and tags. Validate automation that depends on branch names. Establish branch lifecycle and cleanup policies."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q37. A Git release pipeline accidentally builds from a shallow clone and cannot calculate the required version number. How do you fix it?",
