        "question": "Q1. A production Terraform apply is about to destroy a critical database because the resource configuration changed. What do you do?",
        "answer": "Stop the apply before approving any destructive action. Inspect the complete terraform plan, resource address, replacement reason, lifecycle settings, and provider changes. Determine whether the change is intentional, caused by a ForceNew argument, or due to an incorrect resource address or configuration. Confirm backups and recovery objectives with the database owner. Use lifecycle protection where appropriate and correct the configuration before generating a new plan. Apply only after independent review. Validate database availability and retain the approved plan and change record."
