      },
      {
        "question": "Q9. A Terraform module update unexpectedly changes production networking resources. How do you investigate?",
        "answer": "Identify the exact module source and version, review its changelog and code diff, and inspect every planned network resource change. Check variable defaults, output changes, resource naming, dependency references, and provider constraints. Compare the module's prior and new behavior using a non-production environment. Pin a known-good module version if the update is responsible. Correct inputs or module code and regenerate the plan. Validate routes, subnets, security rules, and connectivity before applying. Require module upgrade reviews and integration tests."
