      {
        "question": "Q14. A Terraform resource was renamed in configuration and the plan proposes destroy-and-create. How can you avoid unnecessary replacement?",
        "answer": "Confirm that the real cloud resource should remain the same and that only its Terraform address changed. Use a moved block in supported Terraform versions or a carefully reviewed terraform state mv operation to map the old address to the new address. Back up state and coordinate with anyone sharing the backend. Run a plan to verify Terraform recognizes the move without replacing the object. Check dependencies and outputs, then apply only the intended unrelated changes. Keep resource refactoring changes isolated and tested."
