      },
      {
        "question": "Q16. A production Terraform deployment fails because resources are created in the wrong dependency order. How do you fix it?",
        "answer": "Inspect the dependency graph and failed resource operations to identify missing relationships. Terraform infers dependencies from references, but hidden dependencies may require an explicit depends_on. Add dependencies only where a real operational ordering requirement exists, avoiding unnecessary serialization. Check whether provider APIs are eventually consistent and whether a resource needs a readiness check after creation. Test the graph in a non-production environment and regenerate the plan. Validate that the dependent service is fully ready before deployment continues."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q17. A Terraform state file contains sensitive values and was stored in an insecure location. What is your incident response?",
