      },
      {
        "question": "Q21. A Terraform module uses an incorrect default region and creates resources outside the approved region. How would you correct it?",
        "answer": "Stop further applies and identify the provider region, module variables, environment configuration, and resources already created. Inspect the actual cloud locations and assess data residency, network, cost, and security implications. Correct the region input and provider configuration explicitly, then generate a plan. Some resources cannot be moved between regions and may require controlled recreation or migration. Coordinate data and service migration before deleting anything. Add region allowlists and account-region assertions to the pipeline."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q22. Terraform apply fails because a resource name already exists in the cloud account. What is your recovery process?",
