      },
      {
        "question": "Q9. A production sync fails because a PreSync database migration hook fails. What is your recovery plan?",
        "answer": "Inspect the hook Job, pod logs, exit code, events and database connectivity. Determine whether the migration partially changed the schema before retrying; rerunning a non-idempotent migration can cause further damage. Check migration locks, permissions, timeout settings and compatibility with both old and new application versions. Follow the database team's recovery procedure, then rerun only after confirming safe retry behavior. Validate schema state and application compatibility before continuing the deployment."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q10. A PostSync smoke-test hook fails even though all pods are healthy. How do you handle it?",
        "answer": "Separate infrastructure health from application acceptance. Inspect the PostSync Job logs, test endpoint, service DNS, authentication, test data and timeout settings. Confirm whether the test is failing because the release is defective or because the test environment is unavailable. Keep the deployment marked appropriately and do not bypass the gate without incident approval. Correct the failure, rerun the test safely and record evidence that the release meets production acceptance criteria."
      },
      {
        "question": "Q11. ArgoCD prunes a resource that a production team expected to retain. What checks are required?",
