      {
        "number": 23,
        "question": "Ansible fact gathering is slow or fails on a few hosts",
        "answer": "Treat this as an Ansible automation incident: The play spends most of its startup time gathering facts or fails before reaching the first task. Begin with evidence collection: Compare per-host timings and verbose logs; inspect DNS, remote CPU, SSH latency, mount delays, and custom fact scripts. The main cause to confirm is this: A slow host, blocked network lookup, or expensive custom fact may delay the setup phase. Use a controlled remediation: Gather only the fact subsets the play requires when safe, fix the slow dependency, and avoid disabling facts used later in the play. Before closing the incident, Measure startup time across a representative host sample and verify every variable required by later tasks is still available."
