        "number": 25,
        "question": "A delegated Ansible task runs on the wrong host",
        "answer": "Treat this as an Ansible automation incident: A task intended for a control node or load balancer executes using unexpected variables or connection settings. Begin with evidence collection: Review delegate_to, run_once, inventory_hostname, delegated host variables, and the actual task execution log. The main cause to confirm is this: Delegation changes the execution host, while some variables still refer to the original inventory host. Use a controlled remediation: Make the delegated destination explicit and reference the correct host variables. Use run_once only when one execution is truly intended. Before closing the incident, Run with a one-host limit and verify the operation occurs on the intended delegated machine before widening scope."
