        "number": 26,
        "question": "Ansible serial rollout stops after one batch fails",
        "answer": "Treat this as an Ansible automation incident: Some hosts have been updated, but later batches never start after a failure threshold is reached. Begin with evidence collection: Inspect serial size, max_fail_percentage, failed hosts, completed hosts, and the actual application version on every target. The main cause to confirm is this: Serial execution deliberately limits rollout progression after failures; earlier batches may already be serving changed software. Use a controlled remediation: Pause the rollout, restore or repair the failed batch, and decide whether to continue or roll back based on health evidence. Do not raise the failure threshold blindly. Before closing the incident, Reconcile all hosts to a known version and verify load balancer health before resuming the next batch."
