        "number": 28,
        "question": "Ansible check mode differs from the actual deployment",
        "answer": "Treat this as an Ansible automation incident: A dry run predicts no change or reports a different result from the real playbook execution. Begin with evidence collection: Review check-mode support for each module and inspect command, shell, conditional, registered-result, and template tasks. The main cause to confirm is this: Check mode is a prediction; some modules cannot simulate changes and command tasks may lack a safe simulation. Use a controlled remediation: Use supported modules and explicit check-mode-aware behavior only where its meaning is understood. Test risky operations in staging. Before closing the incident, Compare check-mode output with an observed staging run and document operations that cannot be safely predicted."
