        "answer": "Treat this as an Ansible automation incident: The same role works in one environment but encounters missing files, permission errors, package differences, or connectivity failures in production. Begin with evidence collection: Compare operating system facts, resolved variables, package repositories, service accounts, routes, security policies, and secret versions on paired hosts. The main cause to confirm is this: Production and staging may differ in baseline configuration or dependency versions even when their inventory names look similar. Use a controlled remediation: Correct the actual environment difference and add a compatibility assertion or production-like test. Do not copy all staging configuration into production blindly. Before closing the incident, Canary the correction on a small production group and monitor application health before widening the change."
