      {
        "number": 16,
        "question": "Linux service is active but no process listens on the expected port",
        "answer": "Treat this as a Linux host incident: systemctl reports active, but local or remote clients cannot connect to the configured port. Begin with evidence collection: Inspect ss -lntup, process command line, startup logs, bind address, runtime configuration, and application health. The main cause to confirm is this: The service may have loaded a different port, bound only to loopback, or skipped listener initialization after a dependency error. Use a controlled remediation: Correct the authoritative service configuration and restart or reload through systemd only after validation. Before closing the incident, Test the listener locally and from the intended client network, then confirm load balancer health."
