        "answer": "Treat this as a Linux host incident: The host reports I/O errors, device resets, filesystem warnings, or intermittent read failures. Begin with evidence collection: Collect dmesg and previous-boot journal logs, storage health metrics, device identifiers, and filesystem status. The main cause to confirm is this: A failing device, controller issue, cloud volume problem, or filesystem corruption may be degrading data access. Use a controlled remediation: Protect data and follow the storage provider's recovery guidance; migrate or restore from a healthy replica or backup when required. Before closing the incident, Run approved integrity checks after recovery and verify storage latency and kernel errors no longer recur."
