        "answer": "Treat this as a Linux host incident: The process list shows a defunct process that remains after kill commands are sent. Begin with evidence collection: Use ps -o pid,ppid,state,cmd to identify the zombie and its parent process; inspect the parent's logs and lifecycle. The main cause to confirm is this: A zombie has already exited and remains only because its parent has not collected its exit status. Use a controlled remediation: Fix or safely restart the responsible parent process so it reaps the child. Sending more signals to the zombie itself will not remove it. Before closing the incident, Confirm the zombie entry disappears and monitor the parent for repeated unreaped children."
